{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-19482","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19868","text":"PRISM × box-and-box — Arithmetic Integration Review"}]},{"id":"blk-19483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19869","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-19870","text":" review (no scoring break) · "},{"id":"spn-19871","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-19872","text":" "},{"id":"spn-19873","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-19874","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-19875","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-19876","text":" how the PRISM benchmark engine (OS-009) relates to the [&] governance kernel, which parts of the scoring pipeline are already the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-19877","marks":["bold"],"text":"axiological"},{"id":"spn-19878","text":" rung in disguise, and what additive wiring would make the correspondence exact."}]},{"id":"blk-19484","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19879","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-19485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19880","text":"PRISM *is* the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-19881","marks":["bold"],"text":"axiological rung (rung 2, `score.mjs`) at scale."},{"id":"spn-19882","text":" Where the kernel ranks one decision ("},{"id":"spn-19883","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-19884","text":"), PRISM ranks *systems* across many decisions. The two are the same algebra at different cardinalities, so the integration is mostly "},{"id":"spn-19885","marks":["bold"],"text":"naming + one optional semiring swap"},{"id":"spn-19886","text":", not a rewrite."}]},{"id":"blk-19486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19887","text":"Three concrete touch-points, all additive:"}]},{"id":"blk-19487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19888","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-19889","marks":["bold"],"text":"Composite scoring"},{"id":"spn-19890","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-19891","marks":["code"],"text":"Judge.Aggregator.compute_composite/2"},{"id":"spn-19892","text":") is already a "},{"id":"spn-19893","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability-semiring weighted sum"},{"id":"spn-19894","text":" — name it as rung 2. 2. "},{"id":"spn-19895","marks":["bold"],"text":"Meta-judge \"reject\""},{"id":"spn-19896","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-19897","marks":["code"],"text":"Judge.Aggregator.quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-19898","text":") is already the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-19899","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation / `consume()` veto"},{"id":"spn-19900","text":" — a rejected judgment is annihilated, not averaged. Name it as the deontic floor under the score. 3. "},{"id":"spn-19901","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-pass means"},{"id":"spn-19902","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-19903","marks":["code"],"text":"Sequence.Scorer.per_pass_means/1"},{"id":"spn-19904","text":") use the *arithmetic* mean. An "},{"id":"spn-19905","marks":["bold"],"text":"optional tropical-semiring (min/bottleneck) view"},{"id":"spn-19906","text":" would surface the single weakest dimension — the \"is any rung failing?\" question the kernel's safety floor asks."}]},{"id":"blk-19488","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19907","text":"Rung-by-rung alignment"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-19490","spans":[{"id":"spn-19908","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-19491","spans":[{"id":"spn-19909","text":"PRISM construct"}]},{"id":"blk-19492","spans":[{"id":"spn-19910","text":"Already aligned?"}]}],"id":"blk-19489","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-19493","spans":[{"id":"spn-19911","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-19912","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-19913","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-19494","spans":[{"id":"spn-19914","text":"scenario/transcript = the observable facts being judged"}]},{"id":"blk-19495","spans":[{"id":"spn-19915","text":"✅ (the L1 evidence layer)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19496","spans":[{"id":"spn-19916","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-19917","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-19918","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-19497","spans":[{"id":"spn-19919","text":"the whole CL-dimension scoring pipeline"}]},{"id":"blk-19498","spans":[{"id":"spn-19920","text":"✅ this *is* rung 2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19499","spans":[{"id":"spn-19921","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-19500","spans":[{"id":"spn-19922","text":"meta-judge "},{"id":"spn-19923","marks":["code"],"text":"reject"},{"id":"spn-19924","text":" → drop from aggregate (veto)"}]},{"id":"blk-19501","spans":[{"id":"spn-19925","text":"✅ approximated by "},{"id":"spn-19926","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19502","spans":[{"id":"spn-19927","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-19503","spans":[{"id":"spn-19928","text":"closed-loop "},{"id":"spn-19929","marks":["code"],"text":"loop_closure_rate"},{"id":"spn-19930","text":" slope across passes"}]},{"id":"blk-19504","spans":[{"id":"spn-19931","text":"◻ partial — it's a gradient over time"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19505","spans":[{"id":"spn-19932","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-19506","spans":[{"id":"spn-19933","text":"bootstrap confidence intervals; meta-judge audit"}]},{"id":"blk-19507","spans":[{"id":"spn-19934","text":"✅ uncertainty is first-class"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19508","spans":[{"id":"spn-19935","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-19509","spans":[{"id":"spn-19936","text":"IRT difficulty budget / cost per run"}]},{"id":"blk-19510","spans":[{"id":"spn-19937","text":"◻ implicit"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-19511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19938","text":"(Rungs 5 reflexive and 7 strategic are out of PRISM's remit.)"}]},{"id":"blk-19512","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19939","text":"Concrete alignments (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-19513","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19940","text":"1. Composite = probability-semiring weighted sum (rung 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-19514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19941","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/judge/aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-19942","text":" "},{"id":"spn-19943","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_composite/2"},{"id":"spn-19944","text":" (lines 93–100) computes "},{"id":"spn-19945","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ dim_score × weight"},{"id":"spn-19946","text":". That is precisely the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-19947","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-19948","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-19949","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-19950","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-19951","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-19952","text":", "},{"id":"spn-19953","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-19954","text":"). The CL-dimension weights in "},{"id":"spn-19955","marks":["code"],"text":"Prism.Benchmark.CLCategories.weights()"},{"id":"spn-19956","text":" are the axiological weight vector. No change needed — the recommendation is to *document* that PRISM's composite is the axiological rung evaluated in the probability semiring, so the two systems share one vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-19515","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19957","text":"2. Meta-judge reject = "},{"id":"spn-19958","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-19959","text":" annihilation (deontic floor under the score)"}]},{"id":"blk-19516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19960","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-19961","text":" (lines 131–137) maps a meta-judge recommendation to a weight, and "},{"id":"spn-19962","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregate/3"},{"id":"spn-19963","text":" (line 40) then "},{"id":"spn-19964","marks":["bold"],"text":"filters out"},{"id":"spn-19965","text":" any judgment whose quality weight is "},{"id":"spn-19966","marks":["code"],"text":"0.0"},{"id":"spn-19967","text":". That filter is exactly the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-19968","marks":["bold"],"text":"`consume()` veto / `0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-19969","text":": a rejected judgment does not get *down-weighted and averaged in*, it is "},{"id":"spn-19970","marks":["bold"],"text":"annihilated"},{"id":"spn-19971","text":" — removed from the aggregate entirely. This is the deontic safety floor: a verdict that violates the floor cannot be \"made up for\" by strong scores elsewhere. PRISM already does the right thing; naming it as the "},{"id":"spn-19972","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-19973","text":" rule makes the guarantee legible and testable against law "},{"id":"spn-19974","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-19975","text":" (annihilation) in the kernel's deontic suite."}]},{"id":"blk-19517","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19976","text":"3. Per-pass mean: add an optional tropical (bottleneck) view"}]},{"id":"blk-19518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19977","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-19978","text":" "},{"id":"spn-19979","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_means/1"},{"id":"spn-19980","text":" (lines 82–92) takes the "},{"id":"spn-19981","marks":["bold"],"text":"arithmetic mean"},{"id":"spn-19982","text":" of dimension scores. That answers \"how good on average?\" The kernel's safety floor asks a different question — \"is *any* rung failing?\" — which is the "},{"id":"spn-19983","marks":["bold"],"text":"tropical semiring"},{"id":"spn-19984","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-19985","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-19986","text":") in "},{"id":"spn-19987","marks":["code"],"text":"score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-19988","text":". An *additive* "},{"id":"spn-19989","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_floor/1"},{"id":"spn-19990","text":" companion (the min across dimensions per pass) would expose the bottleneck dimension without touching the existing mean-based metrics. This is the single most useful optional wiring: it turns \"average CL competence\" into \"average "},{"id":"spn-19991","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-19992","text":" weakest-link CL competence,\" matching how the bridge gates on the floor before optimizing the gradient."}]},{"id":"blk-19519","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-19993","text":"4. Loop closure slope = the axiological gradient over time (rung 2 ▸ rung 4)"}]},{"id":"blk-19520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-19994","marks":["code"],"text":"loop_closure_rate/1"},{"id":"spn-19995","text":" (lines 36–40) is the linear-regression slope of per-pass means — literally the "},{"id":"spn-19996","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-19997","text":" the kernel's bridge optimizes in its "},{"id":"spn-19998","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-19999","text":" step, but measured *across time* (which makes it also a temporal-rung, rung-4, liveness signal: \"does the system eventually improve?\"). No change; worth citing the correspondence so \"loop closure\" and \"the best gradient\" are understood as the same quantity at different timescales."}]},{"id":"blk-19521","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20000","text":"Suggested (optional, additive) wiring"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-19523","spans":[{"id":"spn-20001","text":"Change"}]},{"id":"blk-19524","spans":[{"id":"spn-20002","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-19525","spans":[{"id":"spn-20003","text":"Risk"}]},{"id":"blk-19526","spans":[{"id":"spn-20004","text":"Value"}]}],"id":"blk-19522","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-19527","spans":[{"id":"spn-20005","text":"Document composite = probability semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-19528","spans":[{"id":"spn-20006","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-20007","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-19529","spans":[{"id":"spn-20008","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-19530","spans":[{"id":"spn-20009","text":"shared vocabulary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19531","spans":[{"id":"spn-20010","text":"Name reject-filter as "},{"id":"spn-20011","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-20012","text":" annihilation"}]},{"id":"blk-19532","spans":[{"id":"spn-20013","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-20014","text":" "},{"id":"spn-20015","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-20016","text":" doc"}]},{"id":"blk-19533","spans":[{"id":"spn-20017","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-19534","spans":[{"id":"spn-20018","text":"legible safety floor"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19535","spans":[{"id":"spn-20019","text":"Add "},{"id":"spn-20020","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_floor/1"},{"id":"spn-20021","text":" (tropical/min view)"}]},{"id":"blk-19536","spans":[{"id":"spn-20022","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence/scorer.ex"}]},{"id":"blk-19537","spans":[{"id":"spn-20023","text":"low (new fn)"}]},{"id":"blk-19538","spans":[{"id":"spn-20024","text":"bottleneck visibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19539","spans":[{"id":"spn-20025","text":"Cite loop-closure ↔ best-gradient"}]},{"id":"blk-19540","spans":[{"id":"spn-20026","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-20027","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-19541","spans":[{"id":"spn-20028","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-19542","spans":[{"id":"spn-20029","text":"conceptual unification"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-19543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20030","text":"None of these change existing outputs, leaderboards, or the 9-dimension weights."}]},{"id":"blk-19544","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20031","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-19545","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20032","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-20033","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-20034","text":" swap the arithmetic mean for tropical by default — the existing composite"}]}],"id":"blk-19546","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-19548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20035","text":"and per-pass-mean metrics are preserved exactly; tropical is an *additional* view."}]},{"id":"blk-19549","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20036","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-20037","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-20038","text":" re-weight any CL dimension or alter IRT calibration."}]}],"id":"blk-19550","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20039","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-20040","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-20041","text":" make PRISM call into the JS kernel at runtime (the kernel is a spec/ref;"}]}],"id":"blk-19552","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-19554","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20042","text":"PRISM stays self-contained Elixir)."}]},{"id":"blk-19555","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20043","text":"Reference"}]},{"id":"blk-19556","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19558","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20044","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-20045","text":" — semirings (tropical/probability/log)"}]}],"id":"blk-19557","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19560","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20046","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/bridge.mjs"},{"id":"spn-20047","text":" — floor-then-gradient, "},{"id":"spn-20048","marks":["code"],"text":"consume()"},{"id":"spn-20049","text":", "},{"id":"spn-20050","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"}]}],"id":"blk-19559","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20051","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/CC2-capability-composition.md"},{"id":"spn-20052","text":" — operators × arithmetics"}]}],"id":"blk-19561","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20053","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/judge/aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-20054","text":" — composite + meta-judge veto (this review's §1–2)"}]}],"id":"blk-19563","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19566","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20055","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-20056","text":" — per-pass means + loop closure (this review's §3–4)"}]}],"id":"blk-19565","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraay3f7xj35rjphyxb5x2t3iknfk3vfa4w4zewj67kwsnos4qgcvda","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}